==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ru|sla-pro|*brỳzgati}}. Of onomatopoeic origin. Compare {{cog|bg|бръ́згам}}, {{cog|cs|brýzhati}}, {{cog|pl|bryzgać}}, {{cog|sl|brízgati}}, {{cog|uk|бризгати}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|бры́згать}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Tatiana Kerbush-брызгать.wav|a=Saint Petersburg}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|бры́згать|impf|pf=бры́знуть,забры́згать}}

# to [[sprinkle]], to [[spray]] {{+obj|ru|acc<someone/something> + ins<with something>}}
#: {{syn|ru|опры́скивать|окропля́ть}}
#: {{uxi|ru|'''Бры́згать''' [[мя́со]] [[вино|вино́м]].|To sprinkle meat with wine.}}

====Conjugation====
{{ru-conj|impf|1a+p|бры́згать}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|бры́згать|impf|pf=бры́знуть,забры́згать}}

# to [[splash]], to [[splatter]] {{+obj|ru|ins<something>}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[искра|И́скры]] '''бры́зжут''' [[в]] [[разный|ра́зные]] [[сторона|сто́роны]].|Sparks splatter to all sides.}}
# {{lb|ru|figuratively}} to [[shed]], to [[exhale]], to [[pour]], to [[spout]]

